    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Structure of the formal imperative («Höflicher Imperativ»)",
     "texto": [
      "To politely address an adult you don't know, or in a professional setting:",
      "1. **Word order:**",
      "The **verb in the Sie form goes in first position**, immediately followed by the pronoun **Sie**:",
      "**Gehen Sie geradeaus!** (Go straight ahead!).",
      "**Nehmen Sie den Bus!** (Take the bus!).",
      "**Fahren Sie mit der U-Bahn!** (Go by subway!).",
      "2. **Separable verbs in the imperative:**",
      "The base verb goes first and the separable prefix travels to the **very end**:",
      "**Biegen Sie an der Bank links ab!** (Turn left at the bank!).",
      "**Steigen Sie am Bahnhof aus!** (Get off at the station!).",
      "3. **The politeness word «bitte»:**",
      "It's usually added after the pronoun «Sie» or at the end to soften the instruction: **Warten Sie bitte hier!** (Please wait here!)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
